---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from 'astro:i18n';
import plugins from '../data/plugins.json';
const tutorialUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/tutorial/');
const installUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/install/');
const pluginsUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/plugins/');
const directoryUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/plugins/directory/');
const auditUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/audit/');
const packsUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/packs/');
const blogUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/blog/');
const vsUrl = getRelativeLocaleUrl('en', '/blog/vs-claude-code/');
const flat = Object.values(plugins).flat();
const totalPlugins = flat.length.toLocaleString('en-US');
const nVerified = flat.filter((p) => p.test === 'verified').length.toLocaleString('en-US');
---
<Base
  title="DeepSeek Harness (DSH) — Install, Tutorial &amp; vs Claude Code | dshbase"
  description="DeepSeek Harness (DSH) explained: open-source everything-is-a-plugin agent framework. Install DSH, follow the tutorial, compare vs Claude Code, and browse verified plugins."
  currentPath="/"
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">DeepSeek Harness · DSH</p>
    <h1>Everything-is-a-plugin <span class="accent">agent framework.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">DeepSeek Harness (DSH) is the open-source agent framework where every capability is a plugin. This is your independent guide — install it, learn it, compare it, and browse the plugin ecosystem.</p>
    <div class="badge-row">
      <span class="badge">&#x1F4E6; <b>npm</b> plugin ecosystem</span>
      <span class="badge">&#x1F680; <b>open source</b></span>
      <span class="badge">&#x2696;&#xFE0F; <b>vs Claude Code</b> — compared</span>
    </div>
    <div class="browsers">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={installUrl}>&#x2B07; Install guide</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={tutorialUrl}>&#x1F4D6; Tutorial &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>What is <span class="accent">DeepSeek Harness?</span></h2>
    <p>DeepSeek Harness (DSH) is a developer-preview agent framework released by DeepSeek in August 2026. Its defining idea is <strong>everything is a plugin</strong> — tools, capabilities, and integrations are installed as npm plugins rather than built into the core. It's positioned as an open-source alternative to <a href={vsUrl}>Claude Code</a> and Claude Cowork.</p>
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="card"><h3>&#x1F9E9; Everything is a plugin</h3><p>Capabilities are npm packages — add what you need, nothing more.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>&#x1F680; Open source</h3><p>Community can fork, audit, and extend the framework.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>&#x1F4E6; npm ecosystem</h3><p>A growing directory of official and community plugins.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>What <span class="accent">Verified</span> means here</h2>
    <p><strong>Verified</strong> on dshbase is not a topic count or a parseable-manifest check. It means we ran a real install test on dsh <code>0.1.0-rc.6</code> — L1–L3 for headless plugins, plus L4 web CDP when L3 reports web-only:</p>
    <div class="grid3">
      <div class="card"><h3>L1 · Install</h3><p><code>dsh plugin add</code> into a clean profile — the package actually installs.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>L2 · Load</h3><p>The profile boots and dumps config with the plugin activated.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>L3 · Headless</h3><p>Headless Q&amp;A exits cleanly. If the plugin is GUI-only (web-only), we do not stop here.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>L4 · Web CDP</h3><p>Required for web-only plugins: live web profile + browser CDP Q&amp;A. Pass → Verified.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:14px">{nVerified} of {totalPlugins} listings are Verified today. Some other catalogs label “verified” when a plugin is merely installable from a manifest — here it means <em>we ran it</em>. See the <a href={auditUrl}>audit methodology</a>, browse the <a href={directoryUrl}>directory</a>, or start from a <a href={packsUrl}>verified-only scene pack</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>Quick <span class="accent">start</span></h2>
    <p>Install DeepSeek Harness and run your first agent in a minute — full steps on the <a href={installUrl}>install guide</a>.</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web</code></pre>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:3080</code> and enter your DeepSeek API key.</li>
      <li>Configure the model under <strong>Settings → Models</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose a workspace, send a task, and watch the agent work.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="info wrap">
    <h2>Guides &amp; <span class="accent">resources</span></h2>
    <div class="grid3">
      <a class="card card-link card-accent" href={tutorialUrl}><span class="cat">Guide</span><h3>DSH tutorial</h3><p>Install, configure, use plugins, and run real tasks — step by step. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={vsUrl}><span class="cat">Compare</span><h3>vs Claude Code</h3><p>Plugins vs MCP, pricing, and which to choose. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={directoryUrl}><span class="cat">Ecosystem</span><h3>Plugin directory</h3><p>{totalPlugins} plugins — {nVerified} install-tested (L1–L4). <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={packsUrl}><span class="cat">Packs</span><h3>Verified scene packs</h3><p>Curated setups — every slot is verified, not just highest stars. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={pluginsUrl}><span class="cat">Build</span><h3>Plugin guide</h3><p>Write your first dsh plugin and register tools. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
      <a class="card card-link" href={auditUrl}><span class="cat">Trust</span><h3>How we audit</h3><p>L1–L4 methodology and transparent pending failures. <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></p></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq wrap">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <details><summary>What is DeepSeek Harness (DSH)?</summary><p>DeepSeek Harness (DSH) is an open-source agent framework from DeepSeek announced in August 2026. Its core idea is that every capability is a plugin installed from npm, making it a flexible alternative to Claude Code.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is DeepSeek Harness free?</summary><p>DeepSeek Harness is open source. The underlying DeepSeek API (for V4-Pro etc.) is paid, at prices set by DeepSeek.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How is DSH different from Claude Code?</summary><p>Architecturally: DSH is everything-is-a-plugin (npm), while Claude Code centers on MCP servers. See the <a href={vsUrl}>full comparison</a>.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What language is this site in?</summary><p>This site is available in English and Chinese — use the language switch in the top-right corner.</p></details>
  </section>
</Base>
